      "summary": "Checks: foundation, model tests (113), point-in-time, ruff check and format, mypy, the full Python suite: all exit 0. Determinism: two reliability runs on the same audit run gave identical results and byte-identical plots (T13). Phase 1 reproduction holds: odd/even adjusted r and k match v0-validated exactly (QB 0.2706/22.23 ... DST 0.4853/8.74); v0 rerun exact. Synthetic tests with known answers: REML recovers k=9 with unequal season lengths (T12); equal group means and pure noise give boundary or k>50, a grid-edge maximum is flagged unconverged (T14); a mid-season trait shift is caught by halves and lags, not odd/even (T23); permutation nulls reject only real signal and center as derived (T24); the planted extreme unit-season is found by influence (T28). A09 components sum back to each cell exactly (max difference 0). Report figures spot-checked against the receipt (claims corrected where the first draft overstated: MoM agreement, boundary share, noise SD, spread ratio, offense-vs-defense ratio).",
